The visual and functional product experience must remain unchanged by this mission.

Before and after implementation, inspect relevant diffs and verify that no unrelated changes have occurred.

Do not:

- Redesign components.
- Reorganize unrelated pages.
- Rewrite product copy.
- Change layout or visual styling.
- Change data values.
- Change formulas.
- Change API business behavior.
- Change authentication or authorization.
- Refactor unrelated modules.

If an infrastructure change requires a minor application-level adjustment, first determine whether it can be achieved without changing product behavior.

If the required adjustment would change business logic or user-facing behavior, do not proceed without explicit authorization.

Do not establish new visual screenshot baselines from an unverified or incorrect UI state.

If visual comparison is useful, use a trusted existing baseline. Otherwise, use limited functional and responsive smoke checks without claiming full visual-regression coverage.

